id: pm-feecbs
title: "Official ecosystem conformance gate: shared quality, security, SDK-boundary, duplication, and install-performance policy"
description: "Turn the ecosystem trust ladder into one reusable, machine-readable conformance gate for every official external pm package and future Verified package, covering source quality through published-artifact runtime proof."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 1
tags[6]: ecosystem,packages,quality,sdk,security,verified-tier
created_at: "2026-07-24T12:02:58.234Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-24T12:06:04.882Z"
author: claude-code-agent
estimated_minutes: 960
acceptance_criteria: "A machine-readable matrix inventories every official external package and future candidate; a reusable package-owned preset or workflow enforces typecheck, lint, complexity, dead-export analysis, tests, coverage, duplication ratchet, production dependency audit, pack verification, isolated install/activate/doctor, and runtime action-contract smoke; shared maintenance logic is versioned once instead of copied across repositories; intentional shared code is documented and large vendored implementations such as pm-graph inside pm-web are replaced by an explicit package/build dependency or separately justified boundary; public SDK imports only use supported exports and subprocess fallback is limited to explicit process boundaries; package service/renderer ownership produces zero unexplained doctor warnings; install latency is measured with a documented budget and retry/noise policy; published npm artifacts and exact default-branch heads are both proven; no quality threshold is weakened and no package feature is removed."
parent: pm-o8um
risk: medium
confidence: high
dependencies[4]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind}:
  pm-92if,related,"2026-07-24T12:03:39.331Z",null,null
  pm-quzx,related,"2026-07-24T12:03:39.331Z",null,null
  pm-usfg,related,"2026-07-24T12:03:39.331Z",null,null
