comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-24T12:02:58.234Z",claude-code-agent,"Duplicate-check evidence: all-status search found pm-vnjh for the shipped external smoke harness, pm-o8um for the open trust ladder, pm-quzx for dependency ranges and duplicate beads/todos homes, pm-92if for core-repo quality, and pm-usfg for the public SDK boundary. None owns a fleet-wide lint, coverage, duplication, dead-code, security, and install-latency conformance floor, so this focused child extends pm-o8um and relates to those canonical owners."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-24T12:06:04.881Z",claude-code-agent,"Current fleet scope is exactly the 18 public repositories pm-beads, pm-brief, pm-changelog, pm-context, pm-csv, pm-gantt-chart, pm-github, pm-graph, pm-jira, pm-linear, pm-ops, pm-presets, pm-slack, pm-slack-standup, pm-starter, pm-todos, pm-ts-starter, and pm-web. The gate should discover this inventory from authoritative catalog metadata so the list cannot silently drift."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-24T12:06:03.261Z",claude-code-agent,"Passing isolated install and runtime smoke proves package reachability, not source maintainability. Verified ecosystem trust needs a second layer that evaluates lint, coverage, duplication, dead exports, dependency policy, published artifacts, service ownership, and install cost across repository boundaries."
