docs[3]{path,scope,note}:
  docs/EXTENSION_AUTHOR_CONTRACTS.md,project,Package author conformance requirements
  docs/EXTENSIONS.md,project,Package lifecycle and extension contracts
  docs/SDK.md,project,Public SDK authoring boundary
body: "The current 18-repository fleet is release-healthy and every published package passed isolated install, activation, doctor blocking checks, and runtime contract exposure. However, none of the 18 repositories declares a lint script or coverage gate; hand-authored TypeScript uses many explicit any annotations; a cross-repository duplicate scan found 42 clone groups and 2,284 duplicated lines, led by 17 copies of the merge-driver preparation script and a vendored pm-graph implementation inside pm-web; several extensions still emit global renderer/service override warnings; package dependency placement and floors vary; and isolated install time has large outliers. The host already owns reusable smoke and SDK authoring primitives. This feature defines one shared preset/workflow and evidence schema so Community, Verified, and Featured labels reflect reproducible package quality rather than repository-local convention. It must compose with pm-quzx rather than duplicate its beads/todos and dependency-range decisions."
